 the 262 144-entry array from `rand()`, invoked `perform_expensive_operations` 0/1/3 times, and compared XOR, 64-bit sum, and boundary elements — 15/15 configurations across seeds `0, 1, 42, 12345, 4294967295` matched exactly (whole-array agreement, not just a digest of one value).\n3. **Full end-to-end `long_exec`** (real 2000 iterations, ~4.5 min per run) for seeds `7` and `4294967295`: stdout is byte-identical (`cmp` clean, matching md5), i.e. `72337063\\n` and `494145113\\n`.\n4. **Performance parity**: Rust 2.71 s vs C 2.82 s for 20 iterations, so the full run does not regress into a timeout.\n\n`c_src/` was not modified (0 files newer than the build)."}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":954,"cache_read_input_tokens":30146,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":954,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":4,"service_tier":"standard"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"c36b2f45-6188-481e-bf1e-4bbdda3321da","uuid":"f7b13b14-4944-464d-a6c8-9cbdda7e8a91","timestamp":"2026-08-17T20:13:55.096Z"}
